text:
I'm working on enabling ESLint for dom/presentation. As part of this, I found some undefined variables in PresentationDataChannelSessionTransport.js, along the lines of:
throw NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE;
This is meant to be:
throw Cr.NS_ERROR_NOT_AVAILABLE;
I'm not sure if there's any actual bugs caused by this, a brief look makes me think it would just be broken developer debug information.

## Audit of Push API
The IDL is out of date!
The proposed change was: 
```
dictionary PushSubscriptionJSON {
  PushSubscriptionKeys keys = null;
}
```
In the latest spec, it is now:
```
dictionary PushSubscriptionJSON {
  record<DOMString, USVString> keys;
}
```
This one doesn't matter. It's the result of a PushSubscription.toJSON(). 
@lina, I couldn't find a bug to update the IDL to match latest spec. Do you have any status on Push API implementation?

